> Small math bridge before Deep Learning
After Andrew Ng ML, add these:

### Exponentials

\[
e^x
\]

### Logarithms

\[
\log(x)
\]

### Sigmoid

\[
\sigma(z)=\frac{1}{1+e^{-z}}
\]

### Softmax

\[
softmax(z_i)=
\frac{e^{z_i}}{\sum_j e^{z_j}}
\]

### Cross-entropy
Understand conceptually:

> how wrong the predicted probability distribution is compared with the target.

### Chain rule + backprop
At this point also watch:

[3Blue1Brown — Backpropagation Calculus](https://www.3blue1brown.com/lessons/backpropagation-calculus/)

This is where calculus becomes directly useful for neural networks.

**Target time:** ~3–4 hours.

