## Phase 5 — Math you add only when you reach GenAI
Do not learn these in advance. Add them when needed.

### Cosine similarity

\[
\cos(\theta)=
\frac{a\cdot b}
{\|a\|\|b\|}
\]

Useful for:
- embeddings
- semantic search
- RAG

### Normalization
Understand scaling vectors and probabilities.

### Attention math

Eventually:

\[
Attention(Q,K,V)=
softmax\left(
\frac{QK^T}{\sqrt{d_k}}
\right)V
\]

At that point, you already have all the required math:

- matrices
- transpose
- matrix multiplication
- dot products
- square roots
- softmax

That is why advanced mathematics is not needed before starting GenAI.

